    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "Dilution The difference between the public offering price\nper share and the net tangible book value (NTBV) per share of Class A common stock after this offering constitutes the dilution to investors\nin this offering. NTBV per share is determined by dividing our NTBV, which is our total tangible assets less total liabilities (including\nthe value of shares of Class A common stock that may be redeemed for cash), by the number of outstanding shares of Class A common stock. The below calculations (A) assume that (i)\nno shares of Class A common stock are issued to stockholders of a potential business combination target as consideration or issuable\nby a post-business combination company, for instance under an equity or employee share purchase plan, (ii) no shares of Class A common\nstock and convertible equity or debt securities are issued in connection with additional financing that we may seek",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
